course: dictionary
lesson: 12654
title: Disregarding: paying no attention
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Disregarding means paying no attention to something, so you ignore it. «Disregarding the warning signs, Sam ran onto the frozen pond.» Sam saw the signs and chose to ignore them. The ending -ing shows the action is happening, so disregard becomes disregarding.
explain: Disregarding can also mean not counting something. «Disregarding the rain, it was a good day for the picnic.» The rain was there, but the sentence asks us to leave it out when we judge the day. In science, a scientist might write «disregarding air resistance» to leave that force out of a calculation.
explain: Ask yourself: is something being ignored, or left out of a count? Clue words help. Words like rules, warnings or cost often mean ignoring. Words like remainder, leftover or calculation often mean leaving out. Try your meaning in the sentence: if «ignoring» or «leaving out» still makes sense, you have got it.
fact: Disregarding means paying no attention to something.
fact: «Disregarding the rules» means ignoring the rules.
fact: Disregarding can also mean not counting or leaving something out, as in «disregarding the remainder».
fact: Disregard is the verb; disregarding is its -ing form.
fact: Disregarding a warning can lead to someone getting hurt, which is why safety rules matter.
exercise: «Disregarding the warning signs, Mia climbed over the fence.» What does disregarding mean here? | Painting | *Ignoring | Reading aloud | Counting carefully
exercise: «Disregarding the rain, the team played the match.» What does disregarding mean here? | *Not letting the rain stop or bother them | Waiting for the rain to stop before they tried | Choosing the wettest spot on the pitch | Hurrying to find an umbrella
exercise: In science, «disregarding air resistance» means: | Measuring the air in the room | *Leaving air resistance out of the calculation | Making the air heavier | Adding air to the test
test: Which word is the -ing form of disregard? | *disregarding | disregarded | disregard | disregards
test: «Disregarding the cost, the school bought new computers.» What does this sentence suggest? | The school counted every penny and then changed its mind | The school asked for a lower price before buying | The school sold its old computers to pay for them | *The school did not let the cost stop it
exam: Which sentence uses disregarding to mean leaving something out of a count? | «Disregarding the rules, the class ran outside.» | «Disregarding his parents, Ali went out.» | «Disregarding the warning, Tom touched the hot pan.» | *«Disregarding the broken cup, the box still holds six good cups.»
